0..78 Comment "// A theory\'s operation written at its type: `oper next : +U[ω] (T -> -F T)`,"
79..150 Comment "// a thunk of curried arrows, is the operation of those inputs and that"
151..228 Comment "// output, `(_ : T) --> T`, as `functor-pair.gandr`\'s record signature writes"
229..307 Comment "// `next`, and so is the value-function alias `T => T` standing for it. A port"
308..383 Comment "// at a builtin type the theory does not declare reads that type, so `read`"
384..460 Comment "// returns an `Integer`. A model gives each as the function it writes for an"
461..474 Comment "// operation."
